      "hints": [
        "Use gradient formula: $\\frac{(3k+5)-(k+3)}{(k+3)-(-3k-1)}$.",
        "Simplify: $\\frac{2(k+1)}{4(k+1)} = \\frac{1}{2}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the gradient formula $m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}$ for points $A$ and $B$:\n$$m_{AB} = \\frac{(3k + 5) - (k + 3)}{(k + 3) - (-3k - 1)} = \\frac{2k + 2}{4k + 4}$$",
        "Factorise and simplify the fraction (valid since $k \\ne -1$):\n$$m_{AB} = \\frac{2(k + 1)}{4(k + 1)} = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}$$\n$$\\text{Since } m_{AB} = \\frac{1}{2} \\text{ contains no } k, \\text{ the gradient is independent of } k$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Coordinate Geometry": "Forms $\\frac{2k+2}{4k+4}$ (M1). Simplifies to $\\frac{1}{2}$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
