      "hints": [
        "Find midpoint $M(1-k, 2k+4)$.",
        "Perpendicular gradient is $-2$.",
        "Form line $y - (2k+4) = -2(x - (1-k)) \\implies y + 2x = 6$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the midpoint $M$ of the line segment $AB$ in terms of $k$:\n$$M = \\left( \\frac{-3k - 1 + k + 3}{2}, \\, \\frac{k + 3 + 3k + 5}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{-2k + 2}{2}, \\, \\frac{4k + 8}{2} \\right) = (1 - k, \\, 2k + 4)$$",
        "Determine the gradient of the perpendicular bisector:\n$$m_\\perp = -\\frac{1}{m_{AB}} = -\\frac{1}{1/2} = -2$$",
        "Form and simplify the equation of the line passing through $M$:\n$$y - (2k + 4) = -2\\left[ x - (1 - k) \\right]$$\n$$y - 2k - 4 = -2x + 2(1 - k) = -2x + 2 - 2k$$\n$$y + 2x = 6 \\quad (\\text{or } y = -2x + 6)$$"
      ],
